cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If LARMORX helped your research, please cite it as below, together with the
  original tools whose methods you used through it (for example ANTs, AFNI,
  FSL, sdcflows or tedana).
type: software
title: "LARMORX: Library of Algorithmic Reimplementations for MRI through Open Rust eXecution"
abstract: >-
  LARMORX is an open-source, cross-platform neuroimaging toolbox that
  reimplements established neuroimaging algorithms and command-line tools in
  Rust, without the original programs or their system dependencies: ports of
  ANTs/ITK, sdcflows and fMRIPrep's resampler, the AFNI tools as exact replicas
  and clean-room originals, and clean-room originals of FSL-compatible tools,
  with exact replicas of FSL's and tedana's tools in separately licensed
  companion packages. Each tool has a Python API (import larmorx), a command
  line that accepts the original program's arguments (larmorx, lx), and a
  validation record that compares it case by case with the original program.
  Results do not depend on the thread count or the platform: the same bits on
  Linux, macOS and Windows.
authors:
